Matthew has 12 toy soldiers. Half of his collection is 12 / 2 = 6 toy soldiers.

He will sell 6 toy soldiers for $5 each, so he will earn 6 * $5 = $30.
He will sell the other 6 toy soldiers for $7 each, so he will earn 6 * $7 = $42.

In total, he will earn $30 + $42 = $72.

\boxed{72}

